**

__

These were the sons of Israel:⁽²⁹⁾ Reuben, Simeon, Levi, and Judah; Issachar and Zebulun;

**

__

These were the sons of David who were born to him in Hebron: The firstborn was Amnon, whose mother was Ahinoam from Jezreel; the second was Daniel, whose mother was Abigail from Carmel;

**

__

the third was Absalom whose mother was Maacah, daughter of King Talmai of Geshur; the fourth was Adonijah, whose mother was Haggith;

**

__

From the descendants of Benjamin: Sallu son of Meshullam, son of Hodaviah, son of Hassenuah;

**

__

From the priests: Jedaiah; Jehoiarib; Jakin;

**

__

Azariah son of Hilkiah, son of Meshullam, son of Zadok, son of Meraioth, son of Ahitub the leader in God’s temple;

**

__

From the Levites: Shemaiah son of Hasshub, son of Azrikam, son of Hashabiah a descendant of Merari;

**

__

Bakbakkar; Heresh; Galal; Mattaniah son of Mika, son of Zikri, son of Asaph;

**

__

The gatekeepers were: Shallum, Akkub, Talmon, Ahiman, and their brothers. Shallum was the leader;

**

__

So the Levites appointed Heman son of Joel; one of his relatives, Asaph son of Berechiah; one of the descendants of Merari,⁽³⁶⁵⁾ Ethan son of Kushaiah;

**

__

The musicians Heman, Asaph, and Ethan were to sound the bronze cymbals;

**

__

Mattithiah, Eliphelehu, Mikneiah, Obed-Edom, Jeiel, and Azaziah were to play the lyres according to the sheminith style,⁽³⁶⁸⁾ as led by⁽³⁶⁹⁾ the director;

**

__

Berechiah and Elkanah were guardians⁽³⁷¹⁾ of the ark;

**

__

Asaph was the leader and Zechariah second in command, followed by Jeiel, Shemiramoth, Jehiel, Mattithiah, Eliab, Benaiah, Obed-Edom, and Jeiel. They were to play stringed instruments; Asaph was to sound the cymbals;

**

__

Joab son of Zeruiah was commanding general of⁽⁴⁹⁵⁾ the army; Jehoshaphat son of Ahilud was secretary;

**

__

Zadok son of Ahitub and Abimelech son of Abiathar were priests; Shavsha⁽⁴⁹⁶⁾ was scribe;

**

__

David said,⁽⁶²⁹⁾ “Of these, 24,000 are to direct the work of the Lord’s temple; 6,000 are to be officials and judges;

